From 7efb30ae5f075aa76c0d31a1a7dbde1b263f1591 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Stew Forster <ci@rdna-boosts.invalid>
Date: Wed, 11 Nov 2026 08:35:47 -0600
Subject: [PATCH 16/16] rdna-boosts: block 16: the UMA GTT expert store -- an
 APU's MoE expert set served from ONE registered, mlocked region, sized by
 -lme

On an integrated GPU "VRAM" and host RAM are one DRAM, so r236 refused the whole
host-expert tier there and upstream disables the expert cache outright: a MoE model
whose expert set exceeds RAM simply cannot run.  This block adds the tier that can:
ONE anonymous region (mmap + MADV_HUGEPAGE, hipHostRegister(Mapped|ReadOnly) once,
mlock'ed, sliced per (tensor, expert)) that the GPU reads in place at 230-233 GB/s.

  * -lme N|auto sizes it (the same flag, units and heat ranking as the discrete
    host-expert budget -- the one command line that carries across).  The store's
    extent is clamped to RLIMIT_MEMLOCK, a model that fits in RAM declines it, and
    a model that cannot fit is REFUSED at load with the fix rather than left to
    swap.
  * The SHAPE follows the budget: a budget that covers the whole expert set PLACES
    it (static, no eviction); a budget below it takes the ARENA (the store is the
    cache's slot storage, the expert tensors stay as holes in the read-only model
    mapping, LFRU residency serves every read, a miss is one buffered pread into the
    vacated slot).  Measured: the arena holds 13.6 GiB less non-reclaimable memory
    than placement at -lme 4 on a 35B, which is what "cap the NON-SWAPPABLE memory
    spent on MoE experts" means on an APU.
  * -lme is also the opt-in for STREAMING: with it a >RAM model runs on whatever the
    lock can hold (measured: a 122B under RLIMIT_MEMLOCK=20 GiB clamps to a 20 GiB
    arena and runs); without it a model whose weights do not fit RAM is refused in
    0.2 s with the fix, never placed and left to swap.
  * The MTP/nextn head is pinned at full residency OUTSIDE that budget (embedded and
    separate-drafter shapes), and one store is shared safely by two models.
  * The fills run on block 12's adaptive host-read transport; the buffered arm reads
    STRAIGHT into the arena slot (no bounce, no H2D); on RDNA3_5 UMA the ladder
    STARTS on that arm (+13.7% warm, +56-67% on a >RAM model).
  * Prefill streams only what is not resident: a D2D for the used experts the store
    holds, ONE coalesced span read + ONE H2D per maximal run of the rest, from 8
    parallel readers (+63-67% prefill on a >RAM model), and the prefill logits are
    unmoved (mean KLD -0.000000, same-top-p 99.990%).

Measured end to end: a 123.45 GiB model runs on this 123 GiB box; text identical in
every arm (627b2ebd7792 / f586785d7183 / 9ccf62ed39c3 / ee95c45231c3 / 347f9f6f715f /
9b259759672f); the tier is inert on a discrete RDNA4 box by measurement (zero GTT
census lines, gate-host-pool.sh 42/42 with this build, throughput within noise).

Kill switches: MOE_EXPERT_GTT=0 (no store at all, the delivery's previous behaviour
byte for byte), MOE_EXPERT_GTT_RO=0 (register writable), MOE_EXPERT_GTT_MLOCK=0 (do
not lock), MOE_EXPERT_GTT_ARENA=0|1 (force the shape), MOE_EXPERT_GTT_PREFILL=0 (the
per-expert prefill copy), MOE_EXPERT_GTT_FILL_DIRECT=0 (the bounce fill).  Gate:
scripts/gate-uma-experts.sh (16 arms, 40 checks), plus scripts/gate-prefill-logits.sh
and scripts/gate-host-pool.sh on the discrete side.  Scope: Linux, integrated GPUs;
every other backend keeps its behaviour (the code is gated on prop.integrated).
